  "intro": "An exponential function $y=ab^x$ changes by a constant FACTOR per step: $a$ is the initial value (at $x=0$) and $b$ is the growth/decay factor. If $b>1$ it grows; if $0<b<1$ it decays. A percent rate $r$ gives $b=1+r$ for growth or $b=1-r$ for decay. Compare with linear functions, which change by a constant AMOUNT. SAT items test writing a model from a description and reading off initial value and factor.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "A population starts at $200$ and triples each year. Write $P(t)$ and find $P(2)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Initial value $200$, factor $3$: $P(t)=200\\cdot 3^t$.",
          "At $t=2$: $P(2)=200\\cdot 3^2=200\\cdot 9$.",
          "Compute: $1800$."
        ],
        "answer": "$P(t)=200\\cdot 3^t$; $P(2)=1800$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "A $\\$500$ investment grows $4\\%$ per year. Write the model.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Growth factor is $b=1+r=1+0.04=1.04$.",
          "Initial value is $500$.",
          "So $V(t)=500(1.04)^t$."
        ],
        "answer": "$V(t)=500(1.04)^t$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "A substance decays to half every hour from $80$ mg. Amount after $3$ hours?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Factor is $\\frac{1}{2}$: $A(t)=80\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^t$.",
          "After $3$ hours: $80\\cdot\\frac{1}{8}=10$.",
          "So $10$ mg remain."
        ],
        "answer": "$10$ mg"
      }
    },
